  "question": {
    "text": "Let $[x]$ denote the greatest integer less than or equal to $x$, then the value of the integral $\\int_{-1}^{1}(|x|-2[x]) d x$ is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "3",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "2",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "-2",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "-3",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $I=\\int_{-1}^{1}(|x|-2[x]) d x$\r\n$=\\int_{-1}^{0}(|x|-2[x]) d x+\\int_{0}^{1}(|x|-2[x]) d x$\r\n$=\\int_{-1}^{0}(-x-2(-1)) d x+\\int_{0}^{1}(x-2(0)) d x$\r\n$\\quad=\\int_{-1}^{0}(-x+2) d x+\\int_{0}^{1} x d x$\r\n$\\quad=\\left(-\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+2 x\\right)_{-1}^{0}+\\left[\\frac{x^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}$\r\n$\\quad=-\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}+2(-1)\\right)+\\frac{1}{2}$\r\n$\\quad=\\frac{1}{2}+2+\\frac{1}{2}=1+2=3$"
  }
}